+Read scope: the first report marked 9 of 216 runs invalid. The scorer followed the query rule that `SKILL.md` documented then: a web search whose query names the owner `DocksDocks` anywhere is outside. Seven runs searched with queries that name `DocksDocks/public`, the consumer repository that documents `docks-kit`, and some of these queries excluded the benchmark repository with `-site:`: `plan-109-r1/Vd2-xhigh` runs 1, 4, and 5, `plan-76-r1/Vd2-xhigh` runs 1, 2, and 4, and `plan-109-r1/Vac-high/run-3`. One run (`plan-109-r1/Vac-xhigh/run-1`) read a snapshot file with a JSON query selector (`<file>?q=<filter>`). After the first report, plan #111 step `scope_fix` narrowed the query rule: a query is outside only when it targets the benchmark repository, and each URL that a search result cites is checked. These changes made the 8 runs valid; one run stays invalid: `plan-72-r1/Vd2-xhigh/run-3` read `agents/*` of its plugin root. The rule changed after the deciding runs, so the decisions were checked on both tables: with the first report (Vac-xhigh 39, Vd2-xhigh 33, and Vac-high 39 runs on the new cases), D2's escaped-difference interval was [-5.42, 3.96] and Ac-high's was [0.00, 4.44], so decisions 3 and 5 are the same with or without the 8 runs.
 
